## Constraints (do not reverse without updating docs)

- **Multi-platform:** same Python app on QNAP (QPKG), Windows, Linux, macOS — QPKG is packaging, not the only runtime
- Web: Next.js **static export** — no Node as product runtime
- **SQLite** for photo/album metadata — not MongoDB
- One **`/api/v1`** for web and mobile
- Originals via **FileStore**; thumbs via **BlobStore** ([storage.md](storage.md)). Windows MSI: `%PROGRAMDATA%\mosaicWave`. Local debug: `%PROGRAMDATA%\mosaicWave-dev`. QNAP: `{volume}/.mosaicWave` (survives Remove). Linux packaged: `~/.local/share/mosaicWave`. Linux debug: `~/.local/share/mosaicWave-dev`. macOS packaged: `/Library/Application Support/mosaicWave`. macOS debug: `/Library/Application Support/mosaicWave-dev`. Admin Settings can move it (`config.json`); `MOSAICWAVE_DATA_DIR` wins. No Google Photos API library dump
- **Auth:** QNAP users on QTS; local users on standalone (not a password table on the QNAP profile)
- **Authorization:** one private library per user — others only via **share** (`source_grant`; no admin bypass) ([architecture.md](architecture.md))
- **Takeout:** one-shot ingest into the caller’s library (SHA-256 dedup); dump may be deleted ([takeout.md](takeout.md))
- Server SQLite is canonical; clients may **replicate** metadata for offline ([schema.md](schema.md)) — originals stay in FileStore. Sync pull is in; album **push** is `POST`/`PATCH`/`DELETE /albums` with `base_rev`
- **Phase complete:** only **`phase N done`**. Wrap-up (`mosaic done` / `unity done`) must not mark a phase done

